42">https://x.com/acjohnston0/status/2105704069461651942</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/10/saturday-assorted-links-581.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=saturday-assorted-links-581">Saturday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/acjohnston0/status/2105704069461651942</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/acjohnston0/status/2105704069461651942</guid><pubDate>Sat, 03 Oct 2026 16:29:20 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Living Science uses an AI agent to reproduce key findings from seminal papers in economics, document what holds up and extend the analysis with newer data]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTmX88iWQAALNou?format=webp&name=large"></p><p>Philipp Heimberger (@heimbergecon) on X</p><p>Very interesting project: Living Science uses an AI agent to reproduce key findings from seminal papers in economics, document what holds up and extend the analysis with newer data. It’s like a follow-up paper with robustness checks and extensions. New paper every week.</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/heimbergecon/status/2105881619618029946">https://x.com/heimbergecon/status/2105881619618029946</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/10/saturday-assorted-links-581.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=saturday-assorted-links-581">Saturday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/heimbergecon/status/2105881619618029946</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/heimbergecon/status/2105881619618029946</guid><pubDate>Sat, 03 Oct 2026 16:29:20 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Joshua Rothman on Garicano’s Messy Jobs]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://www.newyorker.com/culture/open-questions/will-ai-still-take-our-jobs">https://www.newyorker.com/culture/open-questions/will-ai-still-take-our-jobs</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevol